.TH load "" "Administration"
.SH NAME
load \- load device driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB/etc/load \fIfile\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
load -- load device driver
Usage:	/etc/load file
Driver 'file' is usually found in directory '/drv'.
.HE
.B load
loads the loadable device driver stored in
.IR file ,
which must be in the linker's
.B l.out
format, into the running kernel.
.I file
is usually one of the drivers kept in directory
.BR /drv .
.PP
.B load
reads the header of
.IR file ,
checks its magic number, and searches its symbol table for a
configuration-table symbol (one whose name ends in
.BR con_ ).
For each such symbol it reads the referenced configuration structure
and calls the kernel to bind the driver's text and data into memory
and complete the load.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 8n
\fB/drv\fR	directory of loadable drivers
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B ld
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IP "Cannot open \fIfile\fR"
.I file
does not exist or is not readable.
.IP "Not an l.out"
.I file
does not begin with a valid
.B l.out
magic number.
.IP "Configuration table not found"
.I file
contains no configuration-table symbol, so
.B load
does not know how to bind it into the kernel.
.SH NOTES
Only the superuser may usefully run
.BR load ,
since it acts directly on the running kernel.
